course: dictionary
lesson: 5167
title: Islamic and what it describes
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: Islamic is an adjective. It tells you that something belongs to, or is connected with, Islam. Islam is the religion of Muslims, who believe in one God, called Allah. So when you read «Islamic art», you know the art is connected with that religion. Islam is the name of the religion; Islamic is the word that describes things linked to it.
explain: Context helps you check this. «The Islamic calendar follows the moon.» The words calendar and moon are the clues: this is a calendar connected with Islam that is counted by the Moon. Ask yourself: what does the word describe? Here it describes a calendar. Then swap in your meaning: "the calendar connected with Islam follows the moon" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Islamic can describe many things: art, buildings, law, history and culture. «Islamic patterns» are shapes that repeat, often in careful geometric designs. The word tells you where the patterns come from, and that is useful to know when you read about them in a history or art lesson.
fact: Islamic means belonging to or connected with Islam.
fact: Islam is the religion of Muslims, who believe in one God, called Allah, and follow the teachings of the Prophet Muhammad and the Qur'an.
fact: «Islamic art» often uses geometric patterns that repeat.
fact: The Islamic calendar follows the Moon, so its months begin when the thin new crescent moon is seen.
fact: «Islamic years» are counted from 622, when the Prophet Muhammad moved from Mecca to Medina.
exercise: «The Islamic calendar follows the moon.» What does Islamic describe here? | A type of cloud | A map of the desert | A school timetable | *A calendar connected with Islam
exercise: «Islamic patterns» are often found on tiles and walls. What does Islamic mean in «Islamic patterns»? | Very old and broken | *Connected with Islam | Shaped like a star only | Made of gold
exercise: Which word is the name of the religion itself, not a describing word? | *Islam | Islamic | Ramadan | Eid
test: «Islamic years are counted from 622.» What happened in 622? | A date chosen at random by a king | The first Islamic art was painted | *The Prophet Muhammad moved from Mecca to Medina | The moon was first seen from Earth
test: What does «the Islamic world» mean? | *Countries and cultures shaped by Islam | The planet Mars | A world map made of gold | The world of sea animals
exam: «Ramadan comes about 11 days earlier each year.» Why? | Because Ramadan is always in winter | *Because the Islamic calendar follows the Moon, and its year is about 11 days shorter than the sun's year | Because Ramadan has no set date | Because Ramadan moves to the sun's calendar
